--- a/INSTALL_HUD_FADE.txt
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,8 +0,0 @@
-HUD FADE IN PLACE — Unity 6
-
-1. Close Unity, extract this ZIP into the ROOT folder of your Unity project, and allow replacement of the three listed scripts.
-2. Open Unity. The existing scene and prefab references remain intact; you do not need to run a layout tool.
-3. In Play Mode, open and close Settings, Upgrade, Rebirth, Inventory, Shop and Quest, and start a game from the Main Menu. Check that each HUD item stays at its authored scene position, fades smoothly, and cannot receive clicks while hidden.
-4. Adjust Panel Transition Duration and Modal Backdrop Fade Duration in Assets/GameData/UI/MiningUiData.asset. HUD startup reveal uses the existing MiningHudFlyIn Duration and Delay.
-
-CanvasGroup rule: alpha controls visibility; interactable and blocksRaycasts control clicks. During a fade the HUD is not clickable. After a complete fade-in it becomes clickable. No scene (.unity) file, commit or push is included. The old slide fields remain serialized for safe scene compatibility but no longer move the HUD.
diff --git a/INSTALL_PC_HUD.txt b/INSTALL_PC_HUD.txt
deleted file mode 100644
index c96dec6..0000000
--- a/INSTALL_PC_HUD.txt
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,10 +0,0 @@
-PC HUD COMPACT — UNITY 6
-
-1. Exit Play Mode. Extract this ZIP into the ROOT of the Unity project; allow overwriting the listed C# files. No scene is included.
-2. Wait for Unity compilation. Open your gameplay scene (Mining HUD Canvas).
-3. Run Mining Simulator > UI > Arrange Compact PC Gameplay HUD. Run it again if you already applied v2; it repairs the existing authored objects. Save the scene with Ctrl+S.
-4. Test in Play Mode: Settings/SET opens the play-scene settings panel; R toggles Rebirth details; XP and next ore remain inside the top bar; money and gems do not overlap; Hire, Upgrades, Quest, Inventory, Shop remain clickable.
-
-RULE FOR ALL FUTURE HUD CHANGES: Inspect CanvasGroup on the HUD root and buttons. For visible clickable controls keep alpha=1, interactable=true, blocksRaycasts=true. Their Image/Graphic must have Raycast Target enabled (or an enabled child hit target). Check the parent CanvasGroup too. Modal transitions may temporarily change interaction through MiningUiPanelCoordinator.
-
-The menu makes editable scene objects; it never writes SampleScene.unity to this ZIP. No commit or push was performed. Unity Editor runtime testing is required on your machine.
